  [PASS] 67 the LambdaCDM side is not blocked by the same wall, but it is not effortless either: a single textbook NFW (M200 = 1e15, c = 5) supplies 8e12 Msun inside 50 kpc in 3-D, about 1.2e13 projected, which is 0.7 of what strong lensing needs -- the real Frontier Fields close that with high concentration and merging substructure.  The framework has to find the SAME 1.5e13 in BARYONS with a kernel boost of only ~5% there, so the core is where the two pictures differ most and the item was worth asking even though the tables cannot answer it   (NFW 3-D M(<50 kpc) = 7.91e+12 Msun, projected 1.24e+13, against a mean required M_E(<50 kpc) = 1.67e+13 Msun (ratio 0.74))

