  [PASS] M67-3 mutation control -- a wrong a_0 changes the core boost by a measurable amount, so the kernel is genuinely live at these radii and the null result above is about missing DATA and not about an inert kernel   (nu at 50 kpc with M_b = 3e12: 1.356 (canonical), 1.421 (alt), 2.900 (10 a_0))

========================================================================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================================================================
  67 = NOT RUNNABLE, not a null.  The item asks for eta = M_lens/M_framework to +-0.1 at 20-100 kpc; the on-disk
  HFF tables are member photometry (Granata+2026 structural parameters) with no mass column of any kind, 5-36
  members inside 100 kpc, and a stellar term that is 2-16% of the mass strong lensing requires there.
  What would make it runnable, stated so the next pass does not repeat this: (a) a published lens-model
  convergence map or cumulative M(<R) for each cluster, and (b) an X-ray gas profile into the core.  With those
  two the computation is short -- the kernel part is already written above and takes one line per radius.
  Recorded honestly: the parts that COULD be computed from the tables were, and two of them are results in their
  own right -- the kernel boost at 20-100 kpc is not a fixed 23-33% but a function of an unmeasured baryon
  budget, and the framework needs 6-40x (3.6-24x deprojected) the tabulated member stellar mass in the core to
  lens at all, with the kernel contributing only about 5% of it.

